// PLAYTEST: is `DEFEND_AGGRO_WEIGHT` at 7 now overtuned the other way?
//
// It was raised from 4 on 2026-08-09 because against a trained policy the
// old value made bracing *counterproductive* — the enemy walked past the
// tank, because reducing incoming damage is exactly what bracing does. 7 is
// the smallest value that clears the Defend census with margin. Nothing
// says it is the right value to *play*, and this is the fight for deciding
// that.
//
// Built for reading a distribution by eye. Swings per round is
// `battle::attackers_in_group`, which is `ceil(sqrt(n))` *per group* — so a
// single group of four swings only twice, and the way to get more attackers
// without simply piling on damage is two groups, both inside
// `ENGAGED_GROUPS`. Two fours is four swings a round, which is enough to
// see where the fire goes in a round or two of bracing.
//
// Tuned by measurement: 62% player wins, 58% HP remaining, 0.65 companions
// down over 40 reps, ~17 rounds. The first draft (four Drones, one group)
// was a 100% win at 99% HP — two swings a round from an enemy that could
// not hurt anyone, so bracing was pointless and unobservable. Weak species
// stay trivial at *any* zone; it is the composition that had to change.
//
// What to watch: brace one companion and count. A stronger draw is the
// intent. *Every single swing* landing on the bracer is not — that makes
// Defend a hard taunt and turns every fight into the same opening move,
// which is a worse game than the one where it was too weak.
//
// Then try bracing the Sprite specifically. It is the fragile one, and the
// interesting failure is Defend becoming a way to get your weakest
// companion killed.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 12, zone: 3),
    party: [
        (species: "sentinel", level: 9),
        (species: "sprite", level: 9),
        (species: "scrapper", level: 9),
    ],
    opponents: [
        (species: "trojan", count: 4),
        (species: "trojan", count: 4),
    ],
    reps: 1,
    seed: 901,
)
